{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1534275-have-you-left-out-clans-in-your-game","id":1534275,"title":"Have you left out clans in your game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-15T16:30:14-07:00","id":1534275,"title":"Have you left out clans in your game?","content":"This is something I posted in the VTM board and Black Fox had clan specfic cities and I thought it would interesting if any of you followed suit. It would be interesting to create a city that only has the Gangrel, Mekhet and Nosferatu being there and for some reason the Ventrue and Deava can't get a foothold in said city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T16:46:01-07:00","id":1534276,"title":"","content":"In Requiem, unlike in Masquerade, Clans are not as defining a thing in the power situation of a city. In Requiem, it is Covenants that are much more what defines a city. I've had a few games that have had a lack of a certain Covenant or 2 in a city for various reason (the city is controlled by the Carthian's and have kicked out the Invictus entirely [also have weakened the Lancea to a heavy degree] or another was a city where the Circle of the Crone overthrew and removed the Ordo Dracul that was controlling the city originally)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/898-kurasu","name":"kurasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-16T13:28:42-07:00","id":1534303,"title":"","content":"Yes I was thinking that in our game we would have the Invictus, Carthian Movement and Ordo Dracul holding the dominate spots and the Lancea Sanctum was wiped out by perhaps the Lupines and the Circle Of The Crone just barely having a presence what so ever with maybe a trio of Gangrel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T04:22:22-07:00","id":1534331,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27361_11.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27361\" data-vbnamecard=\"27361\">Lysander</a>. Plenty of cities in my Requiem world have one or two Covenants in control with only a small presence (if at all) by the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T06:45:37-07:00","id":1534339,"title":"","content":"It's all up to the kind of stories one wants to tell - one city has the presence and intriguing of all 5 major covenants, another is dominated by one, two or a triad of sorts, while a third domain is a place where circunstances resulted in the preservation and continued success of a clique of covenants mostly lost and forgotten everywhere else.<br /> <br /> With clans that sort of context can be even more varied and slippery. Depending on local history and the ups &amp; downs of what kindred can trace their origins to where one could have not only matters of clans missing or not, but two groups of what many might see/confuse as the same clan in dispute and claiming otherwise, in a situation not dissimilar to the Ventrue &amp; Julii, or the Mekhet &amp; Grettir and perhaps the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Jiang_Shi_(clan)\" target=\"_blank\">Jiangshi</a> or <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Akhud\" target=\"_blank\">Akhud</a>, if one feels like getting the terrain muddy and so much more treacherous.<br /> <br /> Way i enjoy messing with the subject of knowledge and kindred lore/legendry, half the lineages presented in Ancient Bloodlines, Mythologies, VII and Danse Macabre would turn out to be not quite what one got from the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-17-2024, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T13:15:11-07:00","id":1534364,"title":"","content":"Maybe I would go with a Mekhet or Nosferatu ancient that holds a massive grudge against the Ventrue and Deava clans and hunts them down the moment he or she discovers them near the city or in the city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T11:13:02-07:00","id":1534400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1534275-have-you-left-out-clans-in-your-game?p=1534364#post1534364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I would go with a Mekhet or Nosferatu ancient that holds a massive grudge against ....</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe a strange ancient of uncertain lineage but with elements of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Twice-Cursed\" target=\"_blank\">both</a>, that is tracking down its wayward children, &quot;<i>for daring to break <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Children_of_the_Thorns\" target=\"_blank\">its mirrors</a> and steal away with the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mekhet_(VTR)#Clan_Bane\" target=\"_blank\">reflections</a></i>&quot; whatever that means. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T12:51:52-07:00","id":1534406,"title":"","content":"A interesting idea Baaldam of a strange ancient of unknown origins that the other Kindred know about in whispers that worry that it might decide to target them later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T20:07:19-07:00","id":1534426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1534275-have-you-left-out-clans-in-your-game?p=1534406#post1534406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A interesting idea Baaldam of a strange ancient of unknown origins that the other Kindred know about in whispers that worry that it might decide to target them later.</div> </div> </div> </div>The moment you mentioned Nosferatu and Mekhet i just couldn't stop myself thinking &quot;why not some weirdo somewhere in the middle?&quot;, from there my mind went into what could happen if you mix Hollow Mekhet with Nos or Jiangshi weirdness and the snowball just wouldn't stop rolling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T02:57:14-07:00","id":1534437,"title":"","content":"You know, given the way modern cities have expanded in the past few centuries, I could see a version of Requiem where this is just how most cities are.<br /> <br /> Like, a vampire takes a city of 10,000 people in 1700 as their domain. Maybe that can support a childe or two, but nothing too big. As that city then swells over the next two-hundred years to hundreds of thousands of people, there's a lot more space available. And the vampires best able to fill that space are going to be the descendants of that original vampire. So, by today, where the city population is in the millions, the vast majority of the kindred are of the same clan all tracing their lineage back to that first vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T04:39:20-07:00","id":1534484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1534275-have-you-left-out-clans-in-your-game?p=1534437#post1534437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, given the way modern cities have expanded in the past few centuries, I could see a version of Requiem where this is just how most cities are.<br /> <br /> Like, a vampire takes a city of 10,000 people in 1700 as their domain. Maybe that can support a childe or two, but nothing too big. As that city then swells over the next two-hundred years to hundreds of thousands of people, there's a lot more space available. And the vampires best able to fill that space are going to be the descendants of that original vampire. So, by today, where the city population is in the millions, the vast majority of the kindred are of the same clan all tracing their lineage back to that first vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, that was a common assumption of Masquerade about medieval kindred for example. And yeah, first vampire to hypothetically set up a brood and power base first would possibly have an advantage over hungry dead that come later.<br /> <br /> If <i>everything </i>goes right for them, no setbacks with mortal hunters, spontaneously rising undead, other supernaturals, random spirits or less classified weird magical stuff, among other issues, does not ever come into the way. Except it definitely will, because nature abhors a vacuum and butterfly effects are an itch to deal with, always. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What doesn't break you apart can provide chinks or leverage points for the other corpses to get niches and eat up on that starting advantage.<br /> If they don't eat <b>you </b>and your own in the proccess, that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-20-2024, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T08:50:05-07:00","id":1534491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1534275-have-you-left-out-clans-in-your-game?p=1534484#post1534484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Truth be told, that was a common assumption of Masquerade about medieval kindred for example. And yeah, first vampire to hypothetically set up a brood and power base first would possibly have an advantage over hungry dead that come later.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's sorta there, but not really developed. Like, there's the idea that princes are kinda expected to have broods under them, but I don't remember any discussion of that having a lasting impact on the demographics of a domain. Like, even after a prince is killed off or leaves, their brood can still remain even if none of them necessarily becomes prince. So from then on, that prince's descendants are probably going to be a fairly large chunk of that clan's local population. Therefore in turn future generations of that clan are going to be composed of more descendants of that prince.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If <i>everything </i>goes right for them, </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What doesn't break you apart can provide chinks or leverage points for the other corpses to get niches and eat up on that starting advantage. </div> </div> </div>I feel I didn't quite get my concept across. It's not that this single vampire locks down the domain forever as one big family. It's more of an issue of demography. Like, on average, who is better placed to take expanding territory? The childe of an already present vampire, or one moving in? Further, as the descendants of that first vampire increase in number, that increases the number of vampires who can in turn embrace new vampires. So there's a feedback loop of sorts, where the more descendants a vampire has, the more likely it is that even more descendants will be produced.<br /> <br /> Importantly, this doesn't translate into them necessarily even being allies of each other. You could absolutely still have multiple covenants that all hate each other. Maybe the progenitor vampire was killed way back in the 1700s?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...no setbacks with mortal hunters, spontaneously rising undead, other supernaturals, random spirits or less classified weird magical stuff, among other issues, does not ever come into the way. </div> </div> </div>Sure? As I said, this is a variant of Requiem. I mean, the game isn't really designed around bloodlines (in the familial sense rather than the game mechanic). Like, the assumption seems to be that most vampires from the same clan aren't related particularly closely.<br /> <br /> Additionally, this isn't meant to be a universal trend. Like, the descendants of that first vampire to take that domain might have an advantage, but that doesn't mean much if the Strix come in an wipe everyone out. You could absolutely have some cities be bastions of one or two clans (which have largely avoided mass-death incidents), and others be more evenly spread (where the local vampire population has been wiped out at some point or another).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T12:04:05-07:00","id":1534499,"title":"","content":"You could a Invictus House dynasty that controls the princedom that include their childer or someone that shares the same interests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}